% RETRANSITION, bars 65-70 (Tempo I, 3/4). The E of the A minor bar slips to E flat (V of A flat).
% Horn 1 alone over the double basses' and timpani's E flat: the motto's tail E flat-D-D flat-C to B flat.

retrVlnOne = { R2.*5 | r2 es''8(\p^\markup \italic "espr." f''8 | }
retrVlnTwo = { des'2.)\pp | \once \override Staff.Hairpin.circled-tip = ##t des'2.\> | R2.*3\! | r2 es'8(\p^\markup \italic "sul D" f'8 | }  % c076: sul D, as at 22 (Rimsky-Korsakov PDF 26: on a lower string go no higher than the fourth position, the octave or ninth; E flat5 is the ninth of D). Was sul G (c031)  % c096: "unis." dropped (after non div. there is no division to cancel; Adler part 1 PDF 30)
retrVla = { g2.)\pp | \once \override Staff.Hairpin.circled-tip = ##t g2.\> | R2.*4\! | }  % c096: "unis., sul C" moved: sul C now at 64 b3 where the slur starts; 64 is non div., so no unis. is needed (Adler part 1 PDF 30, 64)
retrVc = { bes,2.\pp | \once \override Staff.Hairpin.circled-tip = ##t bes,2.\> | R2.*4\! | }
retrCb = { es,2.\pp~^\markup \italic "4 soli, change bow at will" | es,2.~ | es,2.~ | es,2.~ | es,2.~ | es,2. | }
retrTimp = { R2.*2 | es2.:32\ppp~^\markup \small \italic "near the rim" | es2.:32~ | es2.:32~ | es2:32~ es8 r8 | }  % c056: roll ends on a tied stroke with the horn and bassoons (Adler part 2 PDF 80, Ex. XII-47)  % c146: ppp roll near the rim, ord. at 79 (Adler part 2 PDF 80: "a beautiful pianissimo ... closer to the rim")
retrHnOne = { R2.*2 | \set Staff.soloText = "1. solo" es'2.(\p\<-\tag #'score ^\markup \bold "1. solo"-\tag #'part ^\markup \bold "solo"^\markup \italic "dolce" | d'4\mp\> des'4 c'4 | bes2.~ | bes2)\pp \tweak staff-position #0 r4 | \set Staff.soloText = "1." }  % c115: horn 2 is tacet, so 70's crotchet rest belongs to horn 1 alone and stays in the stave (Gould PDF 49, 51)  % c046: label written out: after horn 2's "2." at 61-62 the part-combiner no longer prints it  % c035: one label, "1. solo"
retrHnTwo = { R2.*5 | \tag #'score s2. \tag #'part R2. | }  % c115: horn 2 tacet; in the score bar 70 is a spacer so horn 1's crotchet rest is the only rest and stays in the stave (Gould PDF 49, 51)
% c043: bassoon 1 enters at 68 a third under horn 1's tail (D-D flat-C over B flat-B flat-A flat), so the tail over the held dominant is the
% 8-7-6-5 / 6-5-4-3 progression and 68 b3 is a passing 6/4 (A flat-C over E flat) into V7 at 69 (A&S PDF 311-314, Ex. 19-14, 19-16).
retrBsnOne = { R2.*3 | \tweak Stem.direction #DOWN bes2(\pp-\tag #'score ^\markup \bold "1." \tweak Stem.direction #DOWN aes4 | g2.) | g2-\tweak stencil ##f \pp r4 | }  % c160: hidden dynamic for MIDI only: this voice had no dynamic of its own, so score.midi played it at LilyPond's default volume 0.71 (louder than ff) against the printed mark (Sebesky PDF 240-241: compare the score with the recorded result)
retrBsnTwo = { R2.*4 | des2.\pp | des2-\tweak stencil ##f \pp r4 | }  % c160: hidden dynamic for MIDI only: this voice had no dynamic of its own, so score.midi played it at LilyPond's default volume 0.71 (louder than ff) against the printed mark (Sebesky PDF 240-241: compare the score with the recorded result)
% c145: the "1." player labels at 67-68 are score-only; a single player's part does not carry the shared-staff label (Adler part 2 PDF 301, Ex. XVIII-10b: the parts drop the score's "1."); Horn 1 keeps "solo"
